       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. This regimen carries a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth, four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day total)\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note on the order. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
